module

-- **Yours (H).** A front-end theorem: what the rule proofs stand on. It arrives
-- as a `sorry` and a signature install leaves it alone.
--
-- **Canonicity** — that evaluating a literal gives a value in normal form.
--
-- The semantics keeps values canonical: bit-vectors reduced modulo their width,
-- maps ordered and without redundant entries. A rule reasoning about a literal
-- needs to know the model produces *that* form, not merely some representative
-- of the same value.
--
-- One theorem per literal kind the calculus has. A calculus over Booleans alone
-- owes only the first; add the others as the signature grows.
--
-- Could arrive proven: canonicity is a property of the SMT-LIB value types,
-- which come from `smt.eos` and are the same for every calculus over ordinary
-- SMT-LIB.
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- What Logos does here
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- `Cpc/Proofs/Canonical/`: **10,083 lines across 11 files** -- against
-- CpcMini's **228 in one**.
--
-- That ratio, 44 to 1, is the sharpest illustration on this list of cost
-- following theories. The one file CpcMini keeps,
-- `Canonical/TypeDefaultBasic.lean`, is byte-identical to Cpc's. Everything
-- else -- `Maps.lean`, `Seq.lean`, `Ops.lean`, `Pump.lean`,
-- `FiniteSoundness.lean` -- exists because CPC has arrays, sequences, strings
-- and sets, each with its own notion of when a value is in normal form.
--
-- A calculus over Booleans owes the one file. Add a theory with structured
-- values and you buy its canonicity development with it.
--
-- **Whether it can be inherited depends on your `smt.eos`.** The statement is
-- about definitions generated from the SMT-LIB semantics, so a proof of it
-- transfers only while that semantics is the stock one — which is exactly what
-- the `logos-smt` entry of `install/defs/profile.conf` records. Supply your own
-- `smt.eos`, change what a type is or what a well-formed model is, and this
-- becomes yours no matter what upstream ships.
public import @CALCULUS@.ModelWf
import all @CALCULUS@.ModelWf

@[expose] public section

namespace Smtm

/-- A Boolean literal evaluates to a canonical value. -/
theorem model_eval_boolean_canonical (M : SmtModel) (b : SmtEval.native_Bool) :
    __smtx_value_canonical (__smtx_model_eval M (SmtTerm.Boolean b)) = true := by
  sorry

end Smtm
